# ***************
# Open boundaries -- Nares Strait 1-km regional run (2026-10-07)
# ***************
# Adapted from pan_AO input/data.obcs (prescribe + balance, same file naming,
# same 33-tracer OBptrFile map). Domain is a 1120 x 360 rectangle, i running
# S->N along the strait:
#   West  (i=1)    North Water / N Baffin Bay    337 wet cells
#   East  (i=1120) Lincoln Sea                   342
#   South (j=1)    Greenland side                185
#   North (j=360)  Ellesmere side                279
# (two wet corners sit on two boundaries; expected).
#
# The index arrays are GENERATED by python/nares_strait/gen_ob_index.py from
# Nares_bathymetry.bin + Nares_shelficeTopo.bin: an edge cell is open only
# where it is wet, 0 = OB_indexUnset elsewhere. Regenerate, do not hand-edit.
#
# Throughflow correction (user, 2026-10-06): the boundary files will carry a
# constant barotropic offset so the 2015-2025 mean through-strait transport is
# 0.85 Sv (Muenchow 2016): +0.46 Sv as uniform normal velocity over the wet
# Lincoln Sea (East) inflow cells, removed over the Baffin (West) cells. Net
# zero, so useOBCSbalance does not undo it. The iceplume installer patched
# obcs_balance_flow.F so plume volume is included in the balance.
#
 &OBCS_PARM01
 useOBCSsponge = .TRUE.,
