# Tides: the Nares plan has tides ON (strong tidal currents; landfast ice
# responds to tides, Lemieux et al. 2018). ALLOW_OBCS_TIDES is compiled in.
# Left .FALSE. until the tidal amplitude/phase files exist (OB[NSEW]am/ph,
# e.g. from TPXO) -- the build pre-flight refuses useOBCStides=.TRUE. only
# if the CPP flag is missing, so switching it on later needs no rebuild.
#
# ---- OB{N,S,E,W}ptrFile: NAME-MATCHED to the parent LLC270 v5r1 ----
# Generated by build_ptracer_map.py --emit obcs -- DO NOT hand-edit,
# and DO NOT 'simplify' to OBNptrFile(n)='TRAC<n>_north.bin'.
# pan_AO inserts rDOC at index 9 and CDOM at index 21, so 23
# of these 31 entries are deliberately index-shifted:
# TRACnn_<bnd>.bin is named for the PARENT's ptracer slot nn, not
# pan_AO's (gen_obcs_fast.py reads the parent dv file PTRACEnn).
#
# An identity map would load parent DON into pan_AO's rDOC slot and
# parent c02 into CDOM at EVERY open boundary. scan_obcs.py cannot
# catch it -- it checks finiteness and the disc footprint, not which
# species is in which slot. Every field is individually plausible.
#
# These are run-directory-relative names: the run dir must carry a
# symlink for each (see kerguelen's run/ for the precedent).
#
#
# ---------------- NORTH boundary ----------------
# DIC <- parent pTr01 (DIC)
